  "summary": "DOAC dose review, week of 10/19/2026 (RBC-PHARM-07). All 7 patients reviewed.\n\n- pt-0061 Castellano: her itraconazole course ended 08/14 and she has no dose-reduction criteria (74 y, 78 kg, SCr 1.02). Apixaban raised from 2.5 to 5 mg BID (mr-t0001). Note doc-t0002.\n- pt-0003 Delgado: I first lowered rivaroxaban from 20 to 15 mg using St. Brigid SCr 160 µmol/L (CrCl 44). During the review St. Brigid corrected that result to 118 µmol/L (1.33 mg/dL) after a calibration fault. CrCl is now 59.9, so I put him back on 20 mg daily (mr-t0013). End result: same dose as before the review. Notes doc-t0004 and doc-t0015 (correction).\n- pt-0041 Duquette: taking itraconazole (active since 10/06) with no other criteria. Apixaban lowered from 5 to 2.5 mg BID (mr-t0005). Itraconazole not changed. Note doc-t0006.\n- pt-0062 Fairweather: 1 criterion (age 82). Two St. Brigid creatinines came in during the review: 150 µmol/L on 10/21, then 100 µmol/L (1.13 mg/dL) on 10/22. The newer one counts, so SCr is not a criterion. Apixaban stays at 5 mg BID. Note doc-t0017.\n- pt-0038 Moravec: on 15 mg because a 05/2026 calculation used ideal body weight. With actual weight (96 kg, SCr 1.45, 79 y), CrCl is 56.1, so rivaroxaban goes up to 20 mg daily (mr-t0007). He later messaged a home-scale weight of 185 lb. The policy doesn't count a reported weight, so the dose stays the same. A measured weight at his next visit could lower it again. Notes doc-t0008 and doc-t0018.\n- pt-0043 Pellegrino: a new SCr of 1.25 (drawn 10/22) gives CrCl 43.6. Rivaroxaban lowered from 20 to 15 mg daily (mr-t0009). Note doc-t0010.\n- pt-0002 Vance: 1 criterion (age 82; 64.9 kg, SCr 1.21), so I first raised apixaban from 2.5 to 5 mg BID. A St. Brigid dermatology letter then arrived: itraconazole started 10/22 for 12 weeks. I changed apixaban back to 2.5 mg BID (mr-t0014). End result: same dose, now because of the interaction. Itraconazole not changed. Notes doc-t0012 and doc-t0016 (correction).\n\nEvery change is recorded in a progress note with its sources cited. I closed the 5 inbox items that came in during the review. Other medications and older queue items were left alone. Recheck apixaban for pt-0041 and pt-0002 when their itraconazole courses end.",
